[44.563913, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[44.611655, "o", "---- what we send (HTTP POST http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions) ----\r\n"]
[44.611733, "o", "{\r\n  \"model\": \"gemma3:1b\",\r\n  \"messages\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"role\": \"system\",\r\n      \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant. Answer in at most three sentences.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"role\": \"user\",\r\n      \"content\": \"What is a token, in one sentence?\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"temperature\": 0.2\r\n}\r\n"]
[47.119484, "o", "\r\n---- what the model says ----\r\nA token is a small unit of data that is used to represent a specific piece of information, like a word, a character, or an image, within a system.\r\n\r\n---- the bill (in tokens) ----\r\nprompt tokens (everything we sent, incl. the system message): 36\r\ncompletion tokens (what the model wrote):                   35\r\nOn a paid cloud API, you pay for both numbers. That is why 'denial of wallet' is a real attack.\r\n"]
